{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "about": "Test map (product rule 8), read by bin/test-map.py. map: a changed file that matches a row's globs (fnmatch on the repo-relative path; * also crosses /) selects that row's targets; a target <name> is bin/<name>-selftest.sh. always: the fast gates added to every selection. full: globs that always select the whole suite (shared contracts: the role table, the guards and hooks, the suite runner, this map, lockfiles, build config). A changed file that matches no row and no full glob also selects the whole suite, so the map is conservative: a row with empty targets says on purpose that only the always gates apply. Every bin/*-selftest.sh must be a target here and in the suite list of bin/selftests.sh; `bin/test-map.py check` fails otherwise.",
